# Delphi OS — line-ending and binary-attribute policy.
# SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT
#
# Canonical line ending is LF everywhere. Delphi is built on Linux (WSL2) with
# the Windows working tree at C:\dev\Delphi. Forcing LF in the working tree
# (eol=lf, not merely text=auto) keeps both trees byte-identical and prevents
# the CRLF/LF churn that otherwise dirties `git status` on the Windows side.
#
# Binary inventory (verified 2026-06-06): the repository currently tracks ZERO
# binary blobs — every file is text (.rs .ts .tsx .toml .md .proto .json .yaml
# .sh .lock .js .html .css .gitkeep .gitignore). The `binary` rules below are
# therefore forward-looking guards, grounded in Delphi's own architecture:
# shell UI assets (icons/fonts) and local model files (GGUF/ONNX per the
# three-tier inference stack). They ensure such files, when added later, are
# never line-ending-converted or rendered as text diffs. SVG is intentionally
# omitted — it is XML text and is correctly handled by the default rule below.

# ── Default ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Auto-detect text; store in the repo and check out in the working tree as LF.
* text=auto eol=lf

# ── Forward-looking binary guards (none tracked today; see header) ───────
# Shell UI raster assets
*.png   binary
*.jpg   binary
*.jpeg  binary
*.gif   binary
*.ico   binary
*.webp  binary
*.bmp   binary
# Fonts
*.woff  binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf   binary
*.otf   binary
# Local model / inference artifacts (three-tier inference stack)
*.gguf  binary
*.onnx  binary
*.wasm  binary
# Misc binary containers
*.pdf   binary
*.zip   binary
*.gz    binary
